  "findings": [
    "Both official final journals directly record May14,2026 sine-die adjournment of the second regular session of the60thLegislature: Senate4:15p.m.,House4:25p.m. The compound row\u2019s May29 date is unsupported and corrected.",
    "Eight retained named2026 histories stop at listed referrals/recommendations/authorship without passage. Nonpassage before second-session adjournment is expressly an inference, not an invented terminal docket event or recorded vote defeating each bill.",
    "SB1488\u2019s April14 entry is Houseprincipal-author Gann coauthorship; its recorded committee referral is February3 Rules then Appropriations. Do not substitute authorship for passage or committee action.",
    "Both2025 title-bill PDFs contain the same two operative sections: naming DataCentersActof2025 and proposed November1,2025 effect. Billnumbers and requestnumbers differ; preserve separate identities and distinguish textual comparison from legal companion equivalence. The combined row\u2019s analytical scope remains unresolved because neither introduced text supplies a substantive infrastructure policy.",
    "House rule6.9 supplies first-to-second-session carryover context only for pending Housebills; it is not applied to Senatecases or used as freestanding proof of bill-specific death."
  ],
